//! The `content` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property replaces content
//! with a generated value. It can be used to define what is rendered inside an element or
//! pseudo-element. For elements, the `content` property specifies whether the element renders
//! normally (`normal` or `none`) or is replaced with an image (and associated "alt" text). For
//! pseudo-elements and margin boxes, `content` defines the content as images, text, both, or none,
//! which determines whether the element renders at all.
//!
//! Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Grammar: normal | none | [ <content-replacement> | <content-list> ] [/ <alt-text> ]? |
//! <element()>
//!
//! Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-content-3/#propdef-content
//!
//! Author guide: https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/content
//!
//! Purpose and value descriptions adapted from MDN contributors (CC-BY-SA-2.5).
//!
//! Additional value descriptions: Microsoft (MIT).
//!
//! Generated from @webref/css 8.7.8. Do not edit.

